  "output": {
    "answer": "No usability research behind them, and I don't claim there is. The panel is four fictional personas, each just a short brief: a device and a job in their own words, not a feature list — for example Dez, 22, phone-only, job 'swipe-fast, not homework.' The point was to avoid pure demographics by anchoring on the job, but the walk itself was simulated, not a real human, and the record doesn't show any interviews or data behind the briefs. Real users only enter through the real-device check after the panel passes.",
